    "visibility" "2"
    "title" "Platform Efficiency Overlay"
    "description" "[h1]Platform Efficiency Overlay[/h1]
See if your factory is actually moving, and where it is stuck - no belt readers required.

[h2]The overlay[/h2]
Every machine, belt, space belt and space pipe is coloured by how much of its capacity it is using.
A green overlay means the belt is keeping up. Red or orange indicates less than 50% throughput is being achieved.

A green dot appears in each square to indicate if the belt is saturated with items.
This helps you to know if items are here, and just not being consumed, or, if nothing is being produced on the belt at all.

[h2]Platform totals[/h2]
Additionally, select any platform to view its total output on the game's own efficiency gauge.

[h2]Using it[/h2]
[list]
[*]Toggle it with the [b]Platform Efficiency[/b] button in the visualization bar, bottom right. It remembers whether it was on.
[*]Nothing is written to your save, so you can remove it at any time.
[*]Requires Shapez Shifter.
[/list]

Source, readme and issue tracker: https://github.com/QuinnBast/Shapez2-Space-Platform-Efficiencies
Licensed under Apache 2.0."
}
